      "thinking": "Let me analyze this fragment. It's page 4 of 4 of an OIML certificate R137/2012-NL1-15.01, issued by NMi (Netherlands).\n\nDocument-level:\n- number: R137/2012-NL1-15.01\n- project_number: 14200712\n- page: 4 of 4 → page_total: 4\n- member_state: The Netherlands\n- scheme: This is R137 (gas meters). Scheme A or B? Not stated in fragment. R137 certificates are typically Scheme A (type evaluation by issuing authority). But since it's not stated, I should omit. Actually the schema says scheme (A|B). The fragment doesn't mention it. Omit per rule 8.\n- date_issued: not present in fragment. Omit.\n- oiml_issuer_id: not stated explicitly in fragment. NMi is the issuing authority but no issuer ID given. Omit or... The NMi logo is present. oiml_issuer_id might be something like \"NMi\" but no explicit ID. I'll omit.\n\nIssuing authority: NMi (Netherlands Measuring Institute). The fragment shows NMi logo. Name: \"NMi\". Address lines not present. person_responsible not present. I could include name \"NMi Certin B.V.\"? No, don't fabricate. Just name: \"NMi\". Actually the logo says NMi. I'll include issuing_authority with name \"NMi\". Hmm, but is that safe? The logo alt text: \"[NMi logo: \"NMi\" with \"+\" inside a circle]\". I'll include name \"NMi\".\n\nThe table 3: Essential characteristics FMR-Dual. This is a matrix table for the FMR-Dual rotary meter (G-value variants).\n\nColumns:\n- Volume* V [dm³] (cyclic volume) — note footnote marker * explained below the table\n- G-value\n- Qmax [m³/h]\n- minimum Qmin [m³/h]\n- Qt [m³/h]\n- maximum ρmax [bar] — wait, ρ is density normally, but \"maximum ρmax [bar]\" — bar is pressure, so it's likely p_max (pressure max) misOCR'd as ρmax. The text says \"maximum ρmax [bar]\". Hmm. In R137 rotary gas meters, max pressure. I'll canonicalize as \"maximum_pressure\" with unit \"bar\". Actually let me keep as the markdown shows: \"maximum ρmax [bar]\". It's ambiguous; I'll use label \"maximum_pressure_pmax\" or just