amily_name \"FMR-Dual\", models list with attributes per model? Schema: models[]: model_id, label, attributes{}. I can put per-model attributes in model_level characteristics instead. I'll give each model model_id like \"FMR-Dual V2.41 G160\" and maybe label \"G160\". Keep attributes empty or minimal. Actually I could put attributes directly in models. The schema allows attributes{}. To avoid duplication, keep models simple with model_id and label, and put values in characteristics.model_level. But the schema example for R60 only has model_id. I'll include attributes too? Duplication risk. I'll keep model_level characteristics as the authoritative matrix and models as id list with label.\n\nActually, maybe include attributes in models for convenience AND model_level? The rules example for R60 doesn't duplicate. I'll just do models with model_id + label, and characteristics.model_level.\n\nModel ids: Use G-value based with volume disambiguation:\n- \"V2.41dm3-G160\"\n- \"V2.41dm3-G250\"\n- \"V3.96dm3-G250\"\n- \"V3.96dm3-G400\"\n- \"V3.96dm3-G650\"\n- \"V6.34dm3-G400\"\n- \"V6.34dm3-G650\"\n\nLabels: \"G160\", \"G250 (V=2.41 dm³)\", etc. Keep simple.\n\nmodel_level entries:\n1. cyclic_volume, unit dm³, values per model: 2.41, 2.41, 3.96, 3.96, 3.96, 6.34, 6.34 with footnote_markers [\"*\"].\n2. qmax m³/h: 250, 400, 400, 650, 1000, 650, 1000.\n3. qmin m³/h: 1, 2.5, 2.5, 4, 4, 4, 6.5.\n4. qt m³/h: 12.5, 20, 20, 32, 32, 32, 50.\n5. maximum_pressure_pmax bar: 21, 21, 21, 21, 12, 21, 21.\n6. diameter_d mm: \"80 or 100\", \"80 or 100\", \"100 or 150\", \"100 or 150\", \"150 or 200\", \"150 or 200\", \"150 or 200\".\n7. basic_transfer_relationship_revolutions: 414.462, 414.462, 252.282, 252.282, 252.282, 157.676, 157.676.\n8. accuracy_class: \"1.0 or 1.5\" all.\n\nWait — check row 5 again: V=3.96, G=650: Qmax=1000, Qmin=4, Qt=32, pmax=12, D=150 or 200, rev 252.282. Yes.\n\nmatrix_tables[0]:\nname: \"Table 3: Essential characteristics FMR-Dual\"\ncolumns: [\"cyclic_volume_v\